{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SytAdmissible","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SytAdmissible","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.YoungTableaux"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.exists_swapAdmissible_of_one_lt_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.exists_swapAdmissible_of_one_lt_card","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L162-L176","doc":"**The gap this file exists to close (bean SW-5).**  A shape with more than one standard tableau\nhas a tableau admitting an adjacent swap.\n\nFeeding this to `SeminormalRep.genMat_ne_scalar` gives the non-degeneracy payload of\n`hoefsmit_seminormal_rep`: some generator is sent to a non-scalar matrix once `dLambda ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.entry_eq_of_no_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.entry_eq_of_no_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L150-L160","doc":"**The filling of a nowhere-admissible tableau is forced by the shape.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag_cellOf_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag_cellOf_eq","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L132-L148","doc":"**A tableau admissible nowhere puts entry `k` on anti-diagonal `k - 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.cellOf_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.cellOf_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L114-L130","doc":"**Entry `1` sits in the corner.**  The base case of the anti-diagonal induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.entry_corner_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.entry_corner_le","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L99-L112","doc":"The corner entry is minimal: `T.entry 0 0 ≤ T.entry i j` for every cell.  Weak rows take\n`(0,0)` to `(0,j)`, strict columns take `(0,j)` to `(i,j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag_cellOf_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag_cellOf_succ","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L69-L97","doc":"**An inadmissible step moves one along the anti-diagonal.**  Sharing a row puts `k+1` one column\nto the right (`sameRow_adjacent`); sharing a column puts it one row down (`sameCol_adjacent`).  Both\nraise `i + j` by exactly one, which is the whole content of the swap-free case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.syt_ext_on_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.syt_ext_on_cells","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L57-L67","doc":"**Two standard tableaux of the same shape that agree on every cell are equal.**  Off the shape\nboth are `0` by the semistandard `zeros` field, so cell-wise agreement is full agreement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag_mk","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.antiDiag","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SytAdmissible.lean#L51-L53","doc":"The anti-diagonal index `i + j` of a cell.  Constant on the diagonals of the Young diagram,\nand the quantity the swap-free argument tracks. ","signatureChunk":0}]}